IMPORT prelude

-- Temasek Polytechnic Act 1990 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a student, a contracting business, a donor or a Board member:
-- who is a registered student (s 2), what the Polytechnic may award and to whom (s 11, Schedule s 11(1)(d)), late-payment charges
-- and their validation (ss 4(2)(c), 4A), contracts and the common seal (ss 12, 13), regulations and the Gazette (s 9, Schedule
-- ss 6(4), 12(2)), ending a student's studies (Schedule ss 6(3)(c), 11(1)(g)), the Students' Union (s 16, Schedule s 19), the
-- Board's size, terms and votes (Schedule ss 5, 8, 9), the Senate quorum (Schedule s 10(3)), the financial year and donations
-- (Schedule ss 14, 17, 18).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation
-- (version in force from 1/4/2024), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/TPA1990.txt. The latest amendment annotated is
-- Act 4 of 2008 (Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008), marked "wef 01/04/2024" at ss 4(2)(c), 4A and Schedule
-- s 6(2)(k), (3)(f); the legislative history gives its commencement as 1 April 2024.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0224 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. SCOPED accordingly. Not encoded: establishment and objects (ss 3, 4(1)), the Board's and Senate's
-- general powers (s 5, Schedule ss 6(1)-(3), 11 other than (d) and (g)), Schools and committees (ss 6, 7), officers and staff (s 8,
-- Schedule ss 2-4), examinations (s 10, Schedule s 13), grants-in-aid and shares (ss 14, 15), the Standing Finance Committee and
-- estimates (Schedule ss 15, 16). No regulations made under the Polytechnic Constitution were retrieved (s 9(5): they are not
-- gazetted and are not subsidiary legislation), so actual fees, late charges, admission rules and discipline rules are unknown.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Temasek Polytechnic Act 1990`

§§ `2 -- registered student`

-- s 2: "'registered student' means a student registered for a course or subject in the Polytechnic leading to the award of a
-- diploma or certificate of the Polytechnic".
GIVEN `registered for a course or subject` IS A BOOLEAN, `the course leads to a Polytechnic diploma or certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a registered student` IF
    `registered for a course or subject` AND `the course leads to a Polytechnic diploma or certificate`

§§ `11 and Schedule s 11(1)(d) -- what may be awarded, and to whom`

-- s 11: the Polytechnic has power "(a) to award diplomas and certificates and any other academic distinctions specified in the
-- regulations; and (b) to provide such lectures and instruction for persons who are not registered students as the Polytechnic may
-- determine, and to grant certificates to those persons."
-- Schedule s 11(1)(d): the Senate decides "which persons have qualified for the award of diplomas, certificates and other marks of
-- distinction".
-- Limb (b) gives non-registered persons CERTIFICATES only. Reading limb (a) as confined to registered students is an INFERENCE from
-- that contrast; so is joining s 11 to Schedule s 11(1)(d) as a single condition. Schedule s 12(1)(b) lets the Senate regulate "the
-- conditions for the award of degrees", but no provision of the Act gives a power to award a degree; it is encoded as no power.
DECLARE Award IS ONE OF
    `a diploma`
    `a certificate`
    `an academic distinction specified in the regulations`
    `a degree`

GIVEN `the award` IS A Award, `the person is a registered student` IS A BOOLEAN, `took lectures as a non-registered person` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Senate decided the person qualified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Polytechnic may confer the award` IF
        `the Senate decided the person qualified`
    AND CONSIDER `the award`
        WHEN `a certificate` THEN `the person is a registered student` OR `took lectures as a non-registered person`
        WHEN `a degree` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE `the person is a registered student`

§§ `4(2)(c) and 4A -- late-payment charges`

-- s 4(2)(c): the Polytechnic may "fix, demand and receive fees and other charges, including charges for the late payment of any
-- such fee or charge" [Act 4 of 2008 wef 01/04/2024].
-- s 4A: "Every amount collected before the date of commencement of the Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008 as, or
-- purportedly as, a charge for the late payment of any fee or charge referred to in section 4(2)(c) shall be deemed to be and always
-- to have been validly collected, and no legal proceedings shall lie or be instituted or maintained in any court of law".
-- The commencement date, 1 April 2024, is taken from the legislative history, which says it "is not part of the Act".
-- Dates are written as numbers YYYYMMDD (an encoding convention).
GIVEN `collected as a late-payment charge` IS A BOOLEAN, `collection date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `proceedings over the collection are barred` IF
    `collected as a late-payment charge` AND `collection date` LESS THAN 20240401

§§ `12 and 13 -- contracts and the common seal`

-- s 12(1): (a) a contract that between private persons would have to be in writing and under seal "may be made on behalf of the
-- Polytechnic in writing under the common seal"; (b) one that would have to be in writing and signed "may be made ... in writing
-- signed by any person acting under the express or implied authority of the Board"; (c) one valid "by parol only" may be made "by
-- parol ... by any person acting under the express or implied authority of the Board". (2): "A contract made according to this
-- section is effectual in law and binds the Polytechnic". (3): it may be varied or discharged in the same manner.
-- s 13(3): courts "are to take judicial notice of the common seal ... and, until the contrary is proved, are to assume that it was
-- duly affixed."
-- s 12 says "may"; whether a contract made otherwise binds is not decided by the text. This rule says only whether s 12(2) applies.
-- Treating a signed writing as also satisfying limb (c) is an INFERENCE.
DECLARE Formality IS ONE OF
    `would need writing under seal`
    `would need signed writing`
    `would be valid by parol`

GIVEN `the seal is affixed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court assumes the seal was duly affixed` IF
    `the seal is affixed` AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)

GIVEN `the formality` IS A Formality, `in writing under the common seal` IS A BOOLEAN, `improper sealing is proved` IS A BOOLEAN, `made by a person with the Board's express or implied authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `in writing signed by that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12 makes the contract binding on the Polytechnic` IF
    CONSIDER `the formality`
    WHEN `would need writing under seal` THEN `the court assumes the seal was duly affixed` `in writing under the common seal` `improper sealing is proved`
    WHEN `would need signed writing` THEN `made by a person with the Board's express or implied authority` AND `in writing signed by that person`
    OTHERWISE `made by a person with the Board's express or implied authority`

§§ `9 and Schedule ss 6(4), 12(2) -- the Constitution, regulations and the Gazette`

-- s 9(2): the Minister may, after consulting the Board, amend the Polytechnic Constitution; (3) every amendment "must be published in
-- the Gazette". (5): "Regulations made under the Polytechnic Constitution need not be published in the Gazette and are not
-- subsidiary legislation."
-- Schedule s 6(4): Board regulations "come into operation on the day on which they are made unless otherwise provided by the Board."
-- Schedule s 12(2): Senate regulations "must be reported to the Board and come into operation not earlier than one semester after the
-- day on which they are made, unless otherwise approved by the Board."
DECLARE Instrument IS ONE OF
    `an amendment of the Polytechnic Constitution`
    `a regulation of the Board`
    `a regulation of the Senate`

GIVEN `the instrument` IS A Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must be published in the Gazette` IF
    CONSIDER `the instrument`
    WHEN `an amendment of the Polytechnic Constitution` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- `the date the Board fixed has arrived` stands for whatever the Board provided or approved; the text gives no default for it.
GIVEN `the instrument` IS A Instrument, `semesters since made` IS A NUMBER, `the Board provided or approved otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN, `the date the Board fixed has arrived` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulation may be in operation` IF
    IF `the Board provided or approved otherwise`
    THEN `the date the Board fixed has arrived`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the instrument`
         WHEN `a regulation of the Board` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a regulation of the Senate` THEN `semesters since made` AT LEAST 1
         OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Schedule ss 6(3)(c), 11(1)(g) -- ending a student's studies`

-- Schedule s 11(1)(g): the Senate may "require any student on academic grounds to terminate his or her studies at the Polytechnic".
-- Schedule s 6(3)(c): the BOARD may by regulations provide for "the welfare, discipline, suspension and expulsion of students".
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `academic grounds`
    `a disciplinary matter`

DECLARE Authority IS ONE OF
    `the Senate`
    `the Board, by its regulations`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A Authority
`who may end the student's studies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `academic grounds` THEN `the Senate`
    OTHERWISE `the Board, by its regulations`

§§ `16 and Schedule s 19 -- the Students' Union`

-- s 16(1): "Despite anything to the contrary in the Societies Act 1966, the provisions of that Act apply to the Temasek Polytechnic
-- Students' Union and its constituent bodies constituted by the regulations." (2): the Minister for societies may by order in the
-- Gazette exempt the Union or a constituent body "from all or any of the provisions ... subject to any conditions".
-- Schedule s 19(3): the Polytechnic "may impose and collect from the students or any class of students such fees as it may determine
-- for the benefit of the Temasek Polytechnic Students' Union and its constituent bodies".
GIVEN `the Union or a constituent body constituted by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted from the provision by Gazette order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Societies Act provision applies to the body` IF
    `the Union or a constituent body constituted by the regulations` AND (NOT `exempted from the provision by Gazette order`)

GIVEN `levied on the students or a class of students` IS A BOOLEAN, `for the benefit of the Union or its constituent bodies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Union fee is within Schedule s 19(3)` IF
    `levied on the students or a class of students` AND `for the benefit of the Union or its constituent bodies`

§§ `Schedule ss 5, 8 -- the Board's size and terms`

-- Schedule s 5(1): a Chairperson, a Deputy Chairperson, the Principal, and "such other persons, not being less than 9 or more than
-- 15". (2): every member except the Principal is appointed by the Minister and, "unless the Minister otherwise directs, holds office
-- for a period of 3 years". s 8: a person filling a vacancy "must be appointed for the remainder of the term of the person's
-- predecessor".
GIVEN `other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the number of other members is lawful` IF
    `other members` AT LEAST 9 AND `other members` AT MOST 15

GIVEN `fills a vacancy` IS A BOOLEAN, `predecessor's remaining years` IS A NUMBER, `the Minister directs otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN, `directed years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the term in years` MEANS
    IF `fills a vacancy` THEN `predecessor's remaining years`
    ELSE IF `the Minister directs otherwise` THEN `directed years`
         ELSE 3

§§ `Schedule s 9 -- Board meetings`

-- Schedule s 9(2): "The quorum at every meeting of the Board is 6 members." (3): decisions "by a simple majority of the votes of the
-- members present and voting except that, in the case of an equality of votes, the Chairperson or, in his or her absence, the Deputy
-- Chairperson of the Board has a casting vote." (5): if both are absent, an elected member presides -- with no casting vote given.
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER, `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `the Chairperson or Deputy Chairperson is present` IS A BOOLEAN, `the casting vote is for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board decision is adopted` IF
        `members present` AT LEAST 6
    AND (    `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
         OR  (`votes for` EQUALS `votes against` AND `the Chairperson or Deputy Chairperson is present` AND `the casting vote is for`))

§§ `Schedule s 10 -- the Senate`

-- Schedule s 10(2): the Senate "must meet at least twice in each semester". (3): "The quorum of the Senate is the smallest number
-- which is not less than one-quarter of the number of members for the time being."
GIVEN `senate members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Senate quorum` MEANS
    IF FLOOR (`senate members` DIVIDED BY 4) TIMES 4 EQUALS `senate members`
    THEN FLOOR (`senate members` DIVIDED BY 4)
    ELSE FLOOR (`senate members` DIVIDED BY 4) PLUS 1

GIVEN `meetings in the semester` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Senate met often enough` IF
    `meetings in the semester` AT LEAST 2

§§ `Schedule ss 14, 17, 18 -- financial year and donations`

-- Schedule s 14: "The financial year of the Polytechnic begins on 1 April each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
-- Result: the calendar year in which the financial year containing the date began.
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year beginning in` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `year` ELSE `year` MINUS 1

-- Schedule s 17(2): "Records must be kept of all donations to the Polytechnic including the names of donors and any special
-- conditions". s 18: property donated "for any specific purpose must be applied and administered in accordance with the purpose ...
-- and must be separately accounted for."
GIVEN `donor and conditions recorded` IS A BOOLEAN, `given for a specific purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `applied to that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `separately accounted for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donation is handled as the Constitution requires` IF
        `donor and conditions recorded`
    AND ((NOT `given for a specific purpose`) OR (`applied to that purpose` AND `separately accounted for`))
